tps://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9232#issuecomment-538778084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9232","id":538778084,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzODc3ODA4NA==","user":{"login":"madkopp","id":6037000,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzcwMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6037000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp","html_url":"https://github.com/madkopp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madkopp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-10-06T19:11:41Z","updated_at":"2019-10-06T19:11:41Z","body":"@bryevdv Awesome, glad this worked out!\r\n\r\nSorry, I was slammed all week, but to be perfectly honest, I wouldn't have been able to put together these tests, anyways (I'm working on understanding all that - if you know of any good resources, I'd be more than appreciative).\r\n\r\nA couple of questions about the tests, though:\r\n\r\n1) It looks like for the tests we use the datetime.utcnow() function to define the max date.  Might it be better to just pick an arbitrary, but fixed date range?  It's always possible that someone's system is set to the wrong date/time, and that utcnow() returns a date before the min date.  It's also possible that their system is set to a date/time WAY in the future, thereby creating such a huge date range that it takes up memory - I may be overthinking things there, though.  Either way, using a fixed date range would alleviate these concerns, and allow you to expand the tests by including dates before/after daylight savings time changes.  Just a thought, I'd be interested in hearing your thoughts on whether these are actually valid concerns.\r\n\r\n2) We haven't done anything to change the system's timezone to test if that functionality holds up.  I looked into this some.  In general it seems like that's possible to do with Python, but you have to start using winAPI calls, and probably something similar in UNIX environments (see https://stackoverflow.com/questions/20256946/how-to-change-system-timezone-using-python-in-windows).  It might not be a good idea to start changing system level things like that, especially not on the TravisCI workers.  Again, though, I'd be interested in hearing your thoughts.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/538778084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/2440012884","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9232#issuecomment-2440012884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9232","id":2440012884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOADqB3M6Rb6RU","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gith